  "title": "Ex 7.4 (⇐) · If a is even, then a² + 4a + 5 is odd",
  "prompt": "Let $a$ be an integer. Exercise 7.4 says $a^2 + 4a + 5$ is odd if and only if $a$ is even. This problem is one direction of that if-and-only-if: prove that if $a$ is even, then $a^2 + 4a + 5$ is odd. Use direct proof. (The forward (⇒) direction is a separate problem.)",
  "answer_format": "A structured proof: let, case, expr and witness steps (notes optional). No final answer box.",
